# Trivy ignore file: vulnerabilities that the team has decided to accept.
#
# THIS FILE IS EMPTY ON PURPOSE. The StockPilot images have no accepted findings, so
# nothing is ignored and every HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability with a fix stops the pipeline.
#
# Rule for adding a line (the security gate must never be silenced without a reason):
#   1. one vulnerability ID per line, e.g. CVE-2099-12345
#   2. a comment on the line above that says WHY it is safe to ignore
#      (for example "the vulnerable function is never called by this app") and who agreed
#   3. an expiry date so the exception is reviewed again, using Trivy's syntax:
#        CVE-2099-12345 exp:2027-01-31
#
# Example of a correct entry (this is a made-up ID, so it is commented out):
#   # StaticFiles is not used by this app; accepted by the team on 2026-10-18
#   # CVE-2099-12345 exp:2027-01-31
